It's a standard French word but is generally considered old-fashioned to speakers of metropolitan French who mainly used the word Velo

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:32.609
As we've seen the French of Quebec has a number of different features that distinguish it from metropolitan French

00:13:32.650 --> 00:13:34.650
But it seems to me that people sometimes

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:38.609
Exaggerate these differences. There are significant differences in accent

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:44.669
But that seems like something that would cease to be much of a problem with significant exposure to it in terms of vocabulary

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:51.900
Quebec has its own informal expressions and slang. But so do other french-speaking areas including Paris in terms of grammar

00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:54.629
There are some little things here and there but nothing too shocking

